  bootwright / logs
      Render the events of a context's current operation, or of --operation, as lines oldest
      first: the operation log merged with every attempt log. --block keeps one block's events;
      --raw prints that block's newest retained adapter output instead, or attempt N's with
      --attempt. --follow prints what is written so far, then streams new events and each
      running block's output, prefixed by its block, until the operation leaves running. --run
      prints a bounded run's output and --install the host's newest controller install output,
      or one named as --install=install-NNNNNN; either follows with --follow. Text output
      escapes every line for the terminal; JSON and YAML carry the exact output bytes. --detail
      full prints each event's full UTC timestamp. It reads under short shared locks and never
      holds a lease an apply waits on.

  Usage
    bootwright logs [flags]

  Command flags
      --attempt    Print attempt N's output with --raw (default: the newest)
      --block      Keep one block's events, or name the block whose output --raw prints
      --follow     Stream new events and running blocks' output until the operation, run or
                   controller install ends
      --install    Print the newest controller install's output, or one named as
                   --install=install-NNNNNN
      --operation  Select an operation by its op- ID (default: the current operation)
      --raw        Print the block's newest retained adapter output instead of events
      --run        Print a bounded run's output, named run-NNNNNN

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright logs --context lab --follow
